From c8635d4441c7dcf2cf0799e6ce6e42917403d85d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cyberneticangel <dylan.fantauzzo7@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:34:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] Linux: the Ryty host libraries build and link natively

- ryty_win32_compat.h/.cpp: the Win32 calls the glue uses, for Linux.
  VirtualQuery reads a cached snapshot of /proc/self/maps; VirtualProtect
  is mprotect; guarded copies use process_vm_readv; module handles come
  from the dynamic loader. GetModuleHandleA(nullptr) is the Windows-layout
  base (load address - 0x10000), so the game patches' base + 0x10000 +
  eboot addresses land on the same code.
- ryty_vendor_linux.cpp: DLSS, DLSS frame generation and FSR 3.1 come as
  Windows DLLs; on Linux they report themselves unavailable.
- Red-zone patching (FIX-074) is Windows-only: Linux delivers signals
  below the 128-byte red zone.
- Stutter diagnostics, write watches, the heap report and the exception
  counter are Windows-only (they sample Windows threads and heaps).
- DllMain becomes a constructor; the first-draw event becomes an
  exported flag (RytyGpuFirstDrawDone) the save data library polls.
- Game patch file handling (GTS-005/006) uses std::filesystem on Linux.
- gen_exports.py: thunks carry their NIDs as global ELF labels (ELF has
  no .def files). Thunk globals are hidden (PC-relative access).
- libSceAjm links the system FFmpeg on Linux (the prebuilt archives are
  not position-independent). ws2_32/iphlpapi only on Windows. The
  stub copy of sceKernelGetSystemSwVersion stays out of libSceNpAuth.
